  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14199609/assets/3f84859100733c56d6381f6ae5c3f5fa55c693621190b3f921e3e1e8f850a4f9.png)\n\nThe curve ${C}_{1}$ has endpoints $A(1,1)$ and $B(-1,-1).$ Calculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)=2x\\,i+(3-2y)\\,j$ through ${C}_{1}$ measured with respect to the unit normal vector ${n}_{1},$ as shown above.\n\n*Hint: You're given that $F$ is source-free, and the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B$ can be parametrized as*\n\n$$\nr=(1-2t)\\,i+(1-2t)\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$",
